{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.binding_carrier_satisfies_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.binding_carrier_satisfies_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.lean#L225-L236","doc":"**The stripped binding period satisfies the C1 kernel.** For the binding\nperiod `p_n = f_n/n` (any `f` with the involution recurrence), its\n`(n−1)!`-strip `b_n = p_n/(n−1)! = f_n/n!` satisfies the proved depth-2\nkernel `(n+2)·b_{n+2} = b_{n+1} + b_n`. This is the classical keystone\nnormalization leg: C1 governs the binding series up to the explicit Gevrey\nnormalization (the geometric prolongation-symbol identification remains\nconjectural). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.binding_period_is_carrier_stripped","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.binding_period_is_carrier_stripped","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.lean#L212-L223","doc":"**Binding period ↔ C1 carrier (the Gevrey strip).** `f_{m+1}/(m+1) =\n(f_{m+1}/(m+1)!)·m!` — the binding period at index `m+1` equals the C1\ncarrier times `m! = (n−1)!`. Over ℚ (a generic field can have\n`(m+1) = 0`); indexed by `m+1` to avoid `ℕ`-subtraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qlift_normalized_kernel_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qlift_normalized_kernel_exists","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.lean#L169-L195","doc":"**The q-lift exists (probe `qlift_kernel_candidate_crosscheck` → proved).**\nOver any field with nonvanishing q-integers, any sequence satisfying the\nq-involution recurrence `f(n+2) = f(n+1) + [n+1]_q·f(n)` has, on the\nq-factorial-normalized carrier `b_n = f_n/[n]_q!`, the EXACT depth-2\nq-difference kernel `[n+2]_q·b_{n+2} = b_{n+1} + b_n` — the q-lift of\n`normalized_classical_kernel_exists` with `c(q) = 1`, no free constant.\nAt `q = 1` (`qint 1 k = k`) this specializes to the classical fibre.\nThe identification of THIS kernel with the GGM eq-49 / prolongation-\nsymbol carrier remains open (`conj:qdifference-kernel-prolongation-\nsymbol`); the diagonal-gauge comparison is the sibling probe's scope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qfact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qfact","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.lean#L164-L167","doc":"q-factorial `[k]_q! = ∏ [j]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.qint","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.lean#L161-L162","doc":"q-integer `[k]_q = Σ_{i<k} qⁱ` (polynomial form — no division, generic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.normalized_classical_kernel_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.normalized_classical_kernel_exists","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.lean#L126-L159","doc":"**The survivor kernel exists at q = 1 (audit §5) — the classical fibre\nof the re-targeted keystone, proved.** On the Gevrey-normalized (EGF)\ncarrier `b n = f n / n!`, the involution recurrence becomes the EXACT\ndepth-2 kernel relation\n    `(n+2)·b_{n+2} = b_{n+1} + b_n` ,\ni.e. the q-difference keystone's confluent (q → 1) shadow is a\nbona-fide bounded-depth (d = 2) kernel — precisely where the raw-OGF\nobstruction above vanishes. This salvages the depth-2 recurrence\ninstinct of the reverted #4129 wiring on its correct carrier: the open\ncontent that remains is the q-LIFT (a `[n+2]_q`-type relation on the\nq-Borel transform) and the identification of its kernel with the\nSW prolongation symbol — stated as `conj:qdifference-kernel-\nprolongation-symbol`, which stays a conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.doubling_of_involution_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.doubling_of_involution_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.lean#L99-L124","doc":"**Doubling from the involution recurrence (abstract).** Any sequence\nsatisfying `f(n+2) = f(n+1) + (n+1)·f(n)` with `f 0 ≤ f 1` doubles from\nthe second step on: `2·f(n+1) ≤ f(n+2)` for `n ≥ 1`. Instantiating\n`f = involutionNumber` (which satisfies the recurrence by `rfl`) feeds\nthe eventual monotonicity of `B n = I(n)/n` used by the exclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.no_bounded_depth_first_order_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.no_bounded_depth_first_order_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.lean#L61-L97","doc":"**The exclusion (audit §4).** The pinned first-order relation\n`n·Bₙ = Σ_{j≤d} sⱼ·B_{n−j}` cannot hold for all large `n` when `B` is\neventually positive and eventually monotone: bounding every `B_{n−j}`\nby `Bₙ` gives `n ≤ Σⱼ |sⱼ|` for every `n ≥ N + d`, contradicting the\narchimedean property. No limits are needed — the absurdity is a single\ninteger exceeding a fixed real bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.first_order_cancellation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.first_order_cancellation","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QDifferenceConfluentObstruction.lean#L44-L59","doc":"**First-order cancellation (audit §3).** Expanding\n`qⁿ·Bₙ(q) = Σⱼ rⱼ(q)·B_{n−j}(q)` to first order at `q = 1` with the\nzeroth order rigid (`rⱼ(1) = δⱼ₀`), the `∂_q Bₙ` contributions appear\nidentically on both sides and cancel: writing `B` for the classical\nvalues, `B'` for the q-derivatives at 1, and `s j` for `∂_q rⱼ|₁`, the\nfirst-order relation `n·Bₙ + Bₙ' = Bₙ' + Σⱼ sⱼ·B_{n−j}` collapses to a\nconstraint on CLASSICAL data only. Generic commutative ring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}